fix-sequence-object-hierarchy: put objects without a parent (sequence objects) in the NULL hierarchy

Classification: spec-deviation bug fix.

FindEmptyObjectSlot() zeroes the whole slot, leaving hierarchy = 0, an
invalid value, for sequence objects (which are in the NULL hierarchy, see
ObjectCreateHashSequence()); TPM2_ContextSave must report TPM_RH_NULL, as
the TCG reference does.

diff --git a/src/Object.c b/src/Object.c
--- a/src/Object.c
+++ b/src/Object.c
@@ -251,6 +251,12 @@ OBJECT* FindEmptyObjectSlot(TPMI_DH_OBJE
 		    // MemorySet(&object->attributes, 0, sizeof(OBJECT_ATTRIBUTES));
 		    MemorySet(object, 0, sizeof(*object)); // libtpms added: Initialize the whole
 							   // object
+		    // tpm-rs differential testing -- spec deviation fix (NOT
+		    // determinism): objects without a parent (sequence objects) are in
+		    // the NULL hierarchy (see ObjectCreateHashSequence()), so
+		    // TPM2_ContextSave must report TPM_RH_NULL, not the invalid value 0
+		    // left by the MemorySet() above (as the TCG reference does).
+		    object->hierarchy = TPM_RH_NULL;
 		    return object;
 		}
 	}
